# RETIRED AND INTENTIONALLY INERT.
#
# Do not install this file as a casaos.service drop-in. Older candidates used
# that pattern to run an Internet-facing listener inside the privileged CasaOS
# management daemon. ReCasaOS now ships an independent, non-root,
# socket-activated recasaos-public-files.service instead.
#
# Before enabling the new recasaos-public-files.socket, remove the old drop-in
# from /etc/systemd/system/casaos.service.d/ and confirm that casaos.service has
# no RECASAOS_PUBLIC_FILE_* environment variables. Removing this file does not
# remove or alter files in /srv/recasaos-public.
#
# The verifier remains a host file at:
#   /etc/recasaos/public-file.verifier
#
# The independent service imports it with LoadCredential=. On systemd 247 the
# service command uses ${CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY}; do not substitute the newer
# %d credential-directory specifier, which requires systemd 251.
#
# This example contains no unit directives by design, so copying it cannot
# re-enable the retired privileged-daemon integration.
